# =============================================================================
# ALERT -> POLICY DIRECT LINKAGE  (full cross-join, cost-tracked, resumable,
# audited by a second, independent LLM)
#
# This is the DIRECT lane, standalone -- NO routed-lane content at all. The
# routed lane (record -> LINKED RSM -> IA_RSM_POLICY_Linkage -> Policy) is a
# different pipeline entirely; nothing here loads IA_RSM_POLICY_Linkage,
# builds parentage, or derives a record -> policy golden chain through it.
# Candidates are, and only ever are, "every published policy, every alert."
#
# WHAT THIS MEANS FOR GOLDEN / RECALL, PLAINLY:
#   GOLDEN_FILE (record -> REGULATION, hand-curated) still loads -- it's used
#   ONLY to pick which alerts to run (SCOPE_MODE="golden"), not to build
#   candidates and not to score recall. Without the routed lane's
#   REG_ID -> POLICY_ID chain, there is no record -> POLICY golden here, so
#   there is no recall number, no scorecard, no confusion matrix in this
#   script. That isn't a bug to route around -- it's the direct consequence
#   of not bringing routed-lane data in. If you get a proper policy-level
#   golden some other way later, scoring can be added back; faking it from
#   regulation-level golden alone would just reproduce the structural
#   over-mapping problem the original file's comments warned about.
#
# WHAT "JUDGED BY AN INDEPENDENT LLM" MEANS HERE ([F]):
#   A second LLM call re-reads each (alert, policy) pair independently --
#   same two texts, none of the first judge's context except its decision --
#   and says whether it AGREES or DISAGREES, and why. This is a genuine
#   second opinion / QC pass, not a comparison against golden (there's no
#   policy-level golden to compare against). Default slice is the AMBIGUOUS
#   MIDDLE: every INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE verdict, plus LINKED/NOT_LINKED
#   verdicts whose relevance_score falls in a borderline band -- exactly the
#   cases most worth a second opinion. Switch AUDIT_SLICE to "all_linked" or
#   "sample" if you'd rather audit something else; see [F].
#
# SECTIONS
#   0.  Imports + paths + run id        0b. Cost ledger
#   A.  Data load (policies, alerts, golden-for-scope-only)
#   A1. Scope                           A2. Validation probe
#   B1. Config + model params           B2. Cost projection
#   P.  Provenance fingerprint
#   C.  Work plan + checkpointed model execution  (the primary judge)
#   E.  LINKED-only convenience output
#   F.  Independent LLM audit layer (second opinion, no golden needed)
#   G.  Wrap-up summary
# =============================================================================


